{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling","id":1119252,"title":"What is it like to play Changling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-22T08:29:56-07:00","id":1119252,"title":"What is it like to play Changling?","content":"It just occurred to me that I know nothing about this game beyond a few of the races, and the basic idea of them being vulnerable to banality. What is a typical game of Changeling like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:59:49-07:00","id":1119259,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what a typical game is like. I've run and played a lot, and they've all been very different. The only constant I can think of is you're likely to get big shifts in mood and theme, possibly within the same session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T09:25:29-07:00","id":1119266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling#post1119252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just occurred to me that I know nothing about this game beyond a few of the races, and the basic idea of them being vulnerable to banality. What is a typical game of Changeling like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The over all theme of the game is a coming of age ceremony. The Fae are creatures of imagination and dreams, which are quite strong during a person's younger years. But as they get older and more mature, they are expected to leave such childish fantasies behind, or else they risk serious complications later on in life.<br /> <br /> This is why it is rare for Changelings to survive past their 30's, as most have succumbed to Banality at that point. The ones who still cling to the dream are usually considered insane by 'normal' society. You ever seen someone in their late 40's using a teddy bear to scare off the Bogeyman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:20:45-07:00","id":1119297,"title":"","content":"But what do you do, exactly? Like in a vampire game, I might slash up an art gallery as a favor to a nosferatu, hunt down a diseased kindred before the CDC blows the masquerade, try to seduce some blood, try to survive a vozhd attack during a siege by those damned Sabbat, or try to salvage a siege after those damned Cammies blow our vozhd to hell.<br /> <br /> What do Changlings DO?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 07-22-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:40:48-07:00","id":1119304,"title":"","content":"They fight dragons, they steal a kiss from a noble, earning the ire of some nobles and the respect of rascals all over the court. They play the political games, trying to embarrass rivals and earn greater glory. They might fight duels for question of honor. They try to live in a world of dreams and tales, all the while having to face the banality of another world full of dreariness that slowly chips away at their existence. They also tell wonderful gossip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:46:03-07:00","id":1119305,"title":"","content":"And save other Changelings from Banality, hunt Chimerical monsters both to save the land and because they can, find lost love, try to live both a mundane and Kithain existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 07-22-2017, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:50:53-07:00","id":1119307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling?p=1119297#post1119297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what do you do, exactly? Like in a vampire game, I might slash up an art gallery as a favor to a nosferatu, hunt down a diseased kindred before the CDC blows the masquerade, try to seduce some blood, try to survive a vozhd attack during a damned Sabbat siege, or try to salvage a siege after those damned Cammies blow our vozhd to hell.<br /> <br /> What do Changlings DO?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Long Story Short:</b> they try to rekindle humanity's imagination.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> When the Technocracy shut off humanity's collective belief in the supernatural, they started a process of slow degradation as science and reasoning came to replace faith and wonderment. The Age of Reason is killing the Fae, which is why their nobles abandoned the human world to retreat to the Dream world. Those who were left behind were forced to bond with human hosts in order to survive.<br /> <br /> The moon landing rekindled humanity's collective belief that anything was possible (temporarily), thus allowing the Fae who had abandoned the world to return to it in full force. But now they're dying out again because humans don't believe in magic anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> While every other splat in the series is trying to make sure humans think they're just a myth, Changelings actively want humans to believe in them again, because that's how they survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tBsXiTDIahA\" data-code=\"tBsXiTDIahA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tBsXiTDIahA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:19:49-07:00","id":1119641,"title":"","content":"Changeling games can be as political as Game of Thrones. Seriously. I got into the novels many years ago because I was preparing a heavily political game and wanted some inspiration. I asked online about political fantasy novels and was directed towards Martin's series (which only had 3 books at that time). Court politics can be just as nasty if you want it to be that way.<br /> <br /> Games can be as fun and silly as kids playing pretend in their backyard. Except the dragons and goblins are real.<br /> <br /> Games can be as epic as an Arthurian legend, seeking out a powerful legendary artifact in the depths of the Dreaming in order to stop a horrible event from happening.<br /> <br /> They can be about very personal issues of redemption from the banal stresses of life, and trying to claw your way back from the depths of despair and boredom. <br /> <br /> They can be about a up and coming indie rock band that tours the country trying to bring a unique creativity to their audiences as a way to stave off the cold winds of the coming endless Winter.<br /> <br /> They can be about fostering nightmares in a city, working in the shadows to bring people into a belief in the fae in order to once again take over as the dark lords the fae were in a forgotten time.<br /> <br /> I've played and ran every one of the original WoD games. None of them have the flexibility and variety in themes that you'll find in Changeling: The Dreaming. Each of the other games has some inherent limitations that keep you to a certain set of styles of play. Yes, there is still a great bit of variety in what you can do in Vampire, Werewolf, Wraith, and Mage. But in my opinion none of them compare to Changeling. It can be epic or personal, hopeful or bleak, silly or nightmarish, political or adventurous, and anything else you can think of.<br /> <br /> What is playing Changeling like? What can you do? That's a harder question to answer than in any other WoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:30:39-07:00","id":1120000,"title":"","content":"To describe is simple: WEIRD<br /> <br /> You can do anything with a decent group in Changeling. My old group had both personal stories of awakening dreamers and they did extremely crazy stuff like successfully cheering up a depressed Malkavian, shooting down a Technocracy satellite with a gremlin-infested dishwasher and when one of my players turned brony, they visited Equestria, because why not, it was fun. They needed a bit of levity after solving that murder case...<br /> <br /> Basically, the game lets you be as mad as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T21:28:07-07:00","id":1120224,"title":"","content":"I would compare it to mage in that it can be very character driven and the chronicle could vary drastically based off of individuals in the motley. It would also work well with pregenerated stories too. Unlike werewolf you don't have a bunch of responsibility by default, but you can. And unlike vampire you don't need humanity everyday to survive and hide in.<br /> <br /> Big difference from all the game lines, except wraith maybe, you have large enough numbers to have armies and large courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:23:00-07:00","id":1120467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling?p=1120000#post1120000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To describe is simple: WEIRD<br /> <br /> You can do anything with a decent group in Changeling. My old group had both personal stories of awakening dreamers and they did extremely crazy stuff like successfully cheering up a depressed Malkavian, shooting down a Technocracy satellite with a gremlin-infested dishwasher and when one of my players turned brony, they visited Equestria, because why not, it was fun. They needed a bit of levity after solving that murder case...<br /> <br /> Basically, the game lets you be as mad as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You think the cyber space (i.e the Internet) is actually a hideout for Changelings?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's it! VR technology is their attempt to create a stabilized artificial Dream World!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:01:34-07:00","id":1123309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling?p=1119297#post1119297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what do you do, exactly? Like in a vampire game, I might slash up an art gallery as a favor to a nosferatu, hunt down a diseased kindred before the CDC blows the masquerade, try to seduce some blood, try to survive a vozhd attack during a siege by those damned Sabbat, or try to salvage a siege after those damned Cammies blow our vozhd to hell.<br /> <br /> What do Changlings DO?</div> </div> </div> </div>well off the top of my head you could, Slash up an art gallery as an entry ritual to the shaodw court ( or a favor to a Leanhaun, plus gooey dark glamor maybe), hunt down a diseased Dauntine before she blows the Eschaet to hell. seduce a Countess, try to sirvive a Thallian attack orchestrated by the shadow court to destabalize the Barony, or try to salavge a seighe in the newlty erupted battle between commoner revolutionaries and the Sidhe Lord. you canb do a lot of similar things, the skin changes a bit and therefore context but thats how i view it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:40:40-07:00","id":1137293,"title":"","content":"I am/was having the same question as you, CajunKhan. I've played all the other games on and off since their introduction, but have never once played a Changeling game... which left me feeling a bit weird, since they're EVERYWHERE but had never once made a cameo or crossover in one of my games. My newest tabletop campaign has a plot that I felt that Changelings could not avoid getting wrapped up in, and my attempts to research the game have been an uphill battle.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for me, a Twitch stream I used to watch that played Exalted just recently switched over to Changeling 20, with a veteran Storyteller and relatively new (to Changeling) players. Now I'm watching their sessions to get a better idea of the flavor of the game, while also enjoying the fact that they explain things to both players and viewers with game/theme questions (And I think they were saying one of the C20 Authors was also hanging out in chat).<br /> <br /> &quot;Changeling: The Streaming&quot; sessions and their Q&amp;As can be found at:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/jonverrall\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/jonverrall\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/jonverrall\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.twitch.tv/jonverrall </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you don't like Twitch, one of the players also hosts just the sessions on her Youtube channel (They just started, so they're only 3 sessions in right now):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/elizabethaneale\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/elizabethaneale\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/elizabethaneale\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/user/elizabethaneale </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T10:18:54-07:00","id":1137353,"title":"","content":"I would say it is a lot like Calvin and Hobbes: The RPG. Calvin is a childling, probably a Nocker, and Hobbes is his chimerical companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12192-rabdos","name":"Rabdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12192_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T22:27:49-07:00","id":1137608,"title":"","content":"The issue of making humans believe in the fae leads some extreme groups to decide to make humans afraid of the fae, which can make some quick and easy conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T14:32:16-07:00","id":1137827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling?p=1119297#post1119297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what do you do, exactly? Like in a vampire game, I might slash up an art gallery as a favor to a nosferatu, hunt down a diseased kindred before the CDC blows the masquerade, try to seduce some blood, try to survive a vozhd attack during a siege by those damned Sabbat, or try to salvage a siege after those damned Cammies blow our vozhd to hell.<br /> <br /> What do Changlings DO?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling has always suffered from too many options in regards to what the game's about. More so than any other WoD game.<br /> <br /> The wider world conflicts are fairly similar to Vampire and Werewolf. You can have courtly politics where Chaos (Unseelie) is pitted against Order (Seelie). You can have hierarchical struggles between the generations (Childling vs Wilder vs Grump) and between the classes (commoner vs noble). You are also struggling to keep the spark of imagination going in a world filled with banality. Inspiring mortals to create art and drawing power from their creations (think a vampire's herd). On a personal level you're trying to balance your mortal life with your fae adventures. Swing too far into one or the other and you're lost. Too much mortal time and your fae self dies; too much fae time and you go permanently insane. You're also fighting the stuff of dreams and legends in the streets. Dragons, knights, other fae, and monsters of all descriptions. <br /> <br /> A quick way to get into the concept is to think of Spider-Man. You know how he's always struggling with his superheroics and his normal life? That's how the changelings are. Constantly bouncing back and forth. With the added wrinkle that most of the monsters they fight cannot be seen by normal people. That bit's complicated. <br /> <br /> A changeling might have to sneak out of the house but they have a pile of homework to do and their parents are extra watchful because the kid's grades have been slipping in the last few months. Once out they might hook up with their oath circle and go slay a dragon that's been camping at a local freehold. The local noble might give you a quest to travel into the dreaming and recover a lost treasure. You might have to rescue a changeling who's been sent to the nuthouse. You might have to baby sit a changeling who's suffered such terrible wounds they've temporarily forgotten their changeling nature, your job being to make sure they eventually remember. You might go to a gallery opening or hit up a new punk band's first show to harvest some glamour. You might have to fight off an un/seelie attack on your freehold, or launch one of your own. The local noble might be tired of all the commoners in the area and declare they're now verboten, so you could either be caught on in a sweep or have to conduct one. The commoners might decide they've had enough of the so-called &quot;nobles&quot; dictating from on high what everyone else has to do and openly revolt against the hierarchy. You might have to fight your way though the imaginary monsters a mentor has accidentally created in a fit of insanity. You might have to investigate the permanent death of a fellow changeling. Establish a new freehold. Rekindle the fires of a dying freehold. Fight back against the gentrification that's tearing the heart out of a community and the glamour producing artists it harbors. You might have to explain to the cops why you're running around with garbage can lids and boffers in the abandoned warehouse. Or you might unleash your changeling glamour and cow a roomful of important mortals. Only to have to sneak back into your room well after midnight and try to talk your way out of being grounded.<br /> <br /> The main conflicts in Changeling are:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Mortal vs Fae.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Unseelie vs Seelie.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Nightmares vs Dreams.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Grumps vs Wilder vs Childlings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Nobles vs Commoners.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Mists vs Bedlam.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 Banality vs Glamour.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u2022 House vs House.<br /> <br /> Any one set of those could easily make for an interesting session, or the theme for a campaign. Throw in multiple sets, and you're onto something epic. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T13:40:45-07:00","id":1138383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1119252-what-is-it-like-to-play-changling?p=1137608#post1137608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue of making humans believe in the fae leads some extreme groups to decide to make humans afraid of the fae, which can make some quick and easy conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the issue is that any of the other splats can very easily prove that they exist, while Changelings can not. Most people can't see them for what they truly are, and even when they can, it's often temporary, which is why it's so difficult and frustrating.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you tell people you're a dragon when you're 8 years old, they might think &quot;aww, that's so cute.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you tell people you're a dragon when you're 16 years old, they might think &quot;Oh, you're a furry.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you tell people you're a dragon when you're 32 years old, they might think &quot;Oh, you're autistic!&quot;<br /> <br /> The older you get, the more difficult it is to maintain a healthy, active life style as a Changeling, because mortal society does not accept that kind of stuff after a certain point.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, a Changeling's essence can take up a new host in the event of their deaths, but I'm unclear as to whether or not this is a true reincarnation, or if the previous Changeling is merely passing the torch to another mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T13:56:18-07:00","id":1138389,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else tend to have the PTBs in Changeling treat the Right of Ignorance pretty seriously, possibly including execution as a penalty depending on the circumstances and who is accused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}